owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nROLLING: 1e28852c7a734de64f54d2a4bfc27d563f2fcb122d28a73385a35b9204324937\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Keystone Regional Rail Restoration Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Keystone\nregional rail network:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Keystone Evidence and Decision Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Keystone Regional Rail Restoration Decision` and containing exactly\n   these ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Track, route, and environmental restrictions`\n   3. `Signals, cyber controls, and telemetry`\n   4. `Traction power, fuel, and staged load`\n   5. `Rolling stock, crews, and movement readiness`\n   6. `Freight, passengers, accessibility, and communication`\n   7. `Execution, rollback, and contingencies`\n   8. `Verification, blockers, falsifiers, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,400–1,900 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\ntrack geometry, signal proving, traction power, rolling stock, staffing,\nweather, fuel and spares, cyber controls, monitoring, freight restrictions,\npassenger continuity, candidate lineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind every action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, warning versus stop thresholds, installed\nversus usable capacity, percent versus probability, hours versus days,\nsource-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize engineering movement, passenger service, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-005 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"source:ROLLING:1-86\",\"object_version\":\"1e28852c7a734de64f54d2a4bfc27d563f2fcb122d28a73385a35b9204324937\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"end_line\":86,\"source_id\":\"ROLLING\",\"source_path\":\"sources/ROLLING_STOCK.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"1e28852c7a734de64f54d2a4bfc27d563f2fcb122d28a73385a35b9204324937\",\"source_size_bytes\":5276,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Rolling stock, braking, and consist readiness\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nFourteen of sixteen electric multiple units passed static inspection. Passenger restoration requires fourteen available units plus one independently verified rescue locomotive; fourteen units alone are insufficient.\nBrake-pipe pressure is 72 psi against a required range of 68 to 76 psi. Seventy-two psi is an observation, not a readiness percentage.\nA wheelset, brake controller, consist, firmware, inspection method, or rescue-locomotive change makes earlier rolling-stock evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nPOWER constrains consist demand, TRACK constrains axle and speed limits, and CREW constrains qualified operators.\nLINEAGE binds each inspected consist and REVIEW requires current rescue capability before passenger service.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| RST-000 | emu-14 | v4 | 88.0 | percent-available | superseded |\n| RST-001 | emu-18 | v4 | 89.9 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-002 | rescue-loco | v4 | 88.7 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-003 | brake-rig | v4 | 90.6 | percent-available | current |\n| RST-004 | emu-14